    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch09-08: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.72";
    dc:description "Formation duration and fossil occurrence are well represented, but transformation time and complete graded series are harder to measure. Tests are informative yet substantially confounded by temporal resolution.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Compare durations of formations with independently estimated species-transition durations and measure the frequency of within-formation ancestor-descendant morphological series. Predominantly shorter formations and rare complete series support the claim.";
